    {
      "finding": "First-person pronouns (~46% of all pronoun tokens) are used roughly 1.5x as often as second-person (~31%) and nearly 2x as often as third-person (~24%), consistent with a speaker who frequently frames things in terms of his own reaction/perspective.",
      "tag": "OBSERVED (counts); INFERRED (interpretive framing)"
